    Load in LM trajectory normally (File > New Molecule > etc.)

    Load in LAMMPS trajectory by sourcing translate_and_rotate.tcl (Extensions > TkConsole > source translate_and_rotate.tcl). You will have to change line 41 to match the path to your .lammpstrj file. Lines 1-174 set up environmental variables, load in the trajectory, and create representations for the various LAMMPS bead types. Lines 175-205 rotate and translate the LAMMPS molecule to line up with the LM molecule.

    Remove the extra frames from the LAMMPS trajectory (source remove_bdryGrow_frames.tcl)

    Remove the extra frames from the LM trajectory (source keep_every_four.tcl)

Oh yeah, make sure when you do steps 3 and 4 that you have the correct molecule set to top (the lammps one for step 3 and the lm one for step 4).

One last thing, in translate_and_rotate.tcl you need to change line 43 to

mol new $molecule_file  waitfor all type lammpstrj step 1

otherwise it only loads in the 3000th frame.